stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> SettingsLoad : iCemEmule.exe starts (mutex Local\Halliburton_iCem_iCemEmule)
    SettingsLoad --> Idle : EmuSettings.Load() complete
    note right of SettingsLoad
        settings-load-at-startup law:
        Load() runs before AutoStartStreams()
        in EmuEngineHost.Run()
    end note

    Idle --> ComOpenRequest : ctl "start com" or ComEnabled=true (autostart)
    Idle --> LanOpenRequest : ctl "start lan" or LanEnabled=true (autostart)

    ComOpenRequest --> ComStreaming : ComSerialEmitter.Open(port) returns ""
    LanOpenRequest --> LanStreaming : AceLanEmitter.Open(adapter) returns ""

    ComOpenRequest --> Idle : Open() returns error
    LanOpenRequest --> Idle : Open() returns error

    ComStreaming --> Idle : ctl "stop com" or Close()
    LanStreaming --> Idle : ctl "stop lan" or Close()

    Idle --> [*] : Shutdown saves emule_config.xml (ctl "quit" or process kill)
    ComStreaming --> [*] : Shutdown
    LanStreaming --> [*] : Shutdown

    note left of Idle
        AutoStartStreams() applies saved
        ComEnabled/LanEnabled once
        immediately after the 1 Hz timer starts
    end note

    note right of Idle
        ctl = operator command channel:
        ControlPipeServer (\\.\pipe\iCemEmule.Control,
        JSON-lines) started before the timer;
        commands dispatch through EmuEngineHost
        (IEmuControl, thread-safe gate);
        ctl "quit" sets the quit event -> Shutdown.
        UI (EmulatorPage in the shell) is a pure
        ctl client — no state lives in the page.
    end note
